## [The AWS advantage in big data analytics](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/big-data-analytics-options/the-aws-advantage-in-big-data-analytics.md)

- [Amazon Kinesis](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/big-data-analytics-options/amazon-kinesis.md): Amazon Kinesis is a platform for streaming data on AWS that makes it easy to load and analyze streaming data.
- [Amazon MSK](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/big-data-analytics-options/amazon-msk.md): Amazon MSK is a fully managed service that makes it easy for you to build and run applications that use Apache Kafka to process streaming data.
- [AWS Lambda](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/big-data-analytics-options/aws-lambda.md): AWS Lambda lets you run code without provisioning or managing servers.
- [Amazon EMR](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/big-data-analytics-options/amazon-emr.md): Amazon EMR is the industry-leading cloud big data platform for processing vast amounts of data using open source tools.
- [AWS Glue](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/big-data-analytics-options/aws-glue.md): AWS Glue is a serverless data integration service that makes it easy to discover, prepare, and combine data for analytics, machine learning, and application development.
- [AWS Lake Formation](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/big-data-analytics-options/aws-lake-formation.md): AWS Lake Formation is an integrated data lake service that makes it easy for you to ingest, clean, catalog, transform, and secure your data and make it available for analysis and machine learning.
- [Amazon Machine Learning](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/big-data-analytics-options/amazon-machine-learning.md): AWS offers the broadest and deepest set of machine learning services and supporting cloud infrastructure, putting machine learning in the hands of every developer, data scientist, and expert practitioner.
- [Amazon DynamoDB](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/big-data-analytics-options/amazon-dynamodb.md): Amazon DynamoDB is a fast, fully-managed NoSQL database service that makes it simple and cost effective to store and retrieve any amount of data, and serve any level of request traffic.
- [Amazon Redshift](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/big-data-analytics-options/amazon-redshift.md): Amazon Redshift is a fast, fully-managed, petabyte-scale data warehouse service that makes it simple and cost-effective to analyze all your data efficiently using your existing business intelligence tools.
- [Amazon OpenSearch Service](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/big-data-analytics-options/elasticsearch.md): (OpenSearch Service) makes it easy to deploy, operate, and scale OpenSearch Service for log analytics, full text search, application monitoring, and more.
- [Amazon Quick](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/big-data-analytics-options/amazon-quicksight.md): Amazon Quick is a scalable, serverless, embeddable, machine learning-powered business intelligence (BI) service built for the cloud.
- [Amazon Compute Services](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/big-data-analytics-options/amazon-compute-services.md): Amazon EC2, with instances acting as AWS virtual machines, provides an ideal platform for operating your own self-managed big data analytics applications on AWS infrastructure.
- [Amazon Athena](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/big-data-analytics-options/amazon-athena.md): Amazon Athena is an interactive query service that makes it easy to analyze data in Amazon S3 using standard SQL.


## [Solving big data problems on AWS](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/big-data-analytics-options/solving-big-data-problems-on-aws.md)

- [Example 1: Queries against an Amazon S3 data lake](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/big-data-analytics-options/example-1-queries-against-an-amazon-s3-data-lake.md): Data lakes are an increasingly popular way to store and analyze both structured and unstructured data.
- [Example 2: Capturing and analyzing sensor data](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/big-data-analytics-options/example-2-capturing-and-analyzing-sensor-data.md): An international air conditioner manufacturer has many large air conditioners that it sells to various commercial and industrial companies.
- [Example 3: sentiment analysis of social media](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/big-data-analytics-options/example-3-sentiment-analysis-of-social-media.md): A large toy maker has been growing very quickly and expanding their product line.


